id: bluetooth_agents_host
label: Bluetooth host agents.md contributions
package: bluetooth_le_host
description: >
  Bluetooth Host API usage contributions for agents.md
category: Bluetooth|Bluetooth Host (Stack)
quality: evaluation
provides:
- name: bluetooth_agents_host
template_contribution:
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_advertiser
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_advertiser_host
    context: |
      # Bluetooth Host for Silicon Labs Series 2 and Series 3 devices
      ## Advertising (host BGAPI)
      - Include `bluetooth_feature_legacy_advertiser` and/or
        `bluetooth_feature_extended_advertiser`; the base feature
        `bluetooth_feature_advertiser` alone is incomplete and will not build.
        Periodic advertising also needs the periodic advertiser feature and uses
        the same advertising set.
      - Before start, create and optionally configure a set:
        - `sl_bt_advertiser_create_set()`
        - [optional] `sl_bt_advertiser_configure()`
        - [optional] `sl_bt_advertiser_set_timing()`
        - [optional] `sl_bt_advertiser_set_tx_power()`
      - Legacy advertising (after create_set):
        - `sl_bt_legacy_advertiser_set_data()` or
          `sl_bt_legacy_advertiser_generate_data()`
        - `sl_bt_legacy_advertiser_start()` or
          `sl_bt_legacy_advertiser_start_directed()`
      - Extended advertising (after create_set):
        - `sl_bt_extended_advertiser_set_data()`,
          `sl_bt_extended_advertiser_set_long_data()`, or
          `sl_bt_extended_advertiser_generate_data()`
        - [optional] `sl_bt_extended_advertiser_set_phy()`
        - `sl_bt_extended_advertiser_start()` or
          `sl_bt_extended_advertiser_start_directed()`
      - Periodic advertising (after create_set):
        - `sl_bt_periodic_advertiser_set_data()` or
          `sl_bt_periodic_advertiser_set_long_data()`
        - `sl_bt_periodic_advertiser_start()`
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_gatt_server
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_gatt_server
    context: |
      ## GATT server
      - For characteristics with value type `user`, handle
        `sl_bt_evt_gatt_server_user_read_request` with
        `sl_bt_gatt_server_send_user_read_response()`.
      - `sl_bt_evt_gatt_server_user_write_request` covers several ATT opcodes;
        dispatch on `att_opcode`:
        - `sl_bt_gatt_write_request`: respond with
          `sl_bt_gatt_server_send_user_write_response()`
        - `sl_bt_gatt_write_command`: no ATT response
        - `sl_bt_gatt_prepare_write_request`: respond with
          `sl_bt_gatt_server_send_user_prepare_write_response()`, echoing
          offset and value
        Missing responses on opcodes that require one cause the ATT
        procedure to time out.
      - Notifications are unacknowledged; indications require a client
        confirmation. Wait for confirmation (or
        `sl_bt_evt_gatt_server_indication_timeout`) before sending another
        indication on that connection.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_sm
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_sm
    context: |
      ## Security Manager
      - Encryption and bonding are different: pairing can encrypt a link
        without storing a long-term bond. Call `sl_bt_sm_set_bondable_mode(1)`
        when bonding (persistent keys) is required.
      - SM requires a bonding database component (builtin is recommended;
        external conflicts with builtin).
      - `sl_bt_sm_configure()` flag bit 3 enables bonding confirmation: the
        app must handle `sl_bt_evt_sm_confirm_bonding` and call
        `sl_bt_sm_bonding_confirm()`. Leave bit 3 clear to skip that step.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_rtos_adaptation
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_rtos_adaptation
    context: |
      ## Bluetooth RTOS adaptation
      - Do not call BGAPI commands or `sl_bt_bluetooth_pend()` from an ISR or
        from any RTOS context that cannot pend (for example some timer tasks).
      - Individual BGAPI calls are thread-safe. Use
        `sl_bt_bluetooth_pend()` / `sl_bt_bluetooth_post()` only when multiple
        commands must run atomically across threads.

ui_hints:
  visibility: never

metadata:
  sbom:
    license: MSLA
root_path: bluetooth_le_host
